Anger is one of the stages of grief as identified by Elizabeth Kubler-Ross. The nurse would first
 
explain this to the spouse. Telling the spouse the patient will get over the phase soon or that the 
diagnosis is difficult to handle is false reassurance and dismissive of the concerns. It is too early to 
consider counseling although the patient may need it later. This is also a yes/no question which is 
not therapeutic. 
